  "interpretation": [
    "Primary result: all chronological test rows, unchanged partition, observed class distribution.",
    "Secondary result (previously unseen feature-vector subset): test rows whose exact V1..V28 + Amount vector appears in neither training nor validation. Same fitted model, same baseline score, same frozen thresholds; nothing was re-tuned or re-trained for it.",
    "If the excluded rows are all non-fraud, every positive stays in the secondary subset and predictions are unchanged, so recall is identical by construction (verified below), and the secondary subset has a higher fraud prevalence.",
    "Because only non-fraud rows are excluded, precision, F1 and average precision can change partly through the change in prevalence. Do not read those differences as a pure measure of leakage.",
    "The secondary subset makes no claim of entity independence, duplicate removal or leakage removal: the data has no entity identifiers, and near-identical vectors that are not byte-equal remain.",
    "Calibration was not evaluated; scores should not be interpreted as validated probabilities. F1 thresholds are a demonstration objective.",
    "No business savings are claimed."
  ],
